{
  "_doc": [
    "The Gradient panel's stop-edit law (transcripts/GRADIENT.md: STOP_OPACITY_COMBO, STOP_LOCATION_COMBO, Combo-driven reorder).",
    "edit_stop(stops, index, field, value) -> (stops, index), or refused (expected: null) when index names no stop, field is not opacity/location, or value is not a number in [0, 100].",
    "opacity: the stop's opacity is set. location: the stop's location is set, then the list is STABLY sorted by location (a tie does not cross), the returned index is the moved stop's new position, and every stop whose next stop (by identity) changed has midpoint_to_next reset to 50.",
    "Stops use the YAML shape {color, opacity, location, midpoint_to_next}. Every input stop here carries midpoint_to_next 40 so a reset is visible.",
    "Read by workspace_interpreter/tests/test_gradient_stop.py (reference), jas_dioxus/src/cross_language_test.rs and JasSwift/Tests/Panels/GradientStopCorpusTests.swift."
  ],
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "opacity_sets_one_stop",
      "_comment": "Opacity is a plain set on the selected stop; order, locations and midpoints are untouched.",
      "stops": [
        {
          "color": "#ff0000",
          "opacity": 100,
          "location": 0,
          "midpoint_to_next": 40
        },
        {
          "color": "#00ff00",
          "opacity": 100,
          "location": 50,
          "midpoint_to_next": 40
        },
        {
          "color": "#0000ff",
          "opacity": 100,
          "location": 100,
          "midpoint_to_next": 40
        }
      ],
      "index": 1,
      "field": "opacity",
      "value": 50,
      "expected": {
        "stops": [
          {
            "color": "#ff0000",
            "opacity": 100,
            "location": 0,
            "midpoint_to_next": 40
          },
          {
            "color": "#00ff00",
            "opacity": 50,
            "location": 50,
            "midpoint_to_next": 40
          },
          {
            "color": "#0000ff",
            "opacity": 100,
            "location": 100,
            "midpoint_to_next": 40
          }
        ],
        "index": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "opacity_on_unsorted_stops_keeps_their_order",
      "_comment": "A document can carry stops out of location order (an imported gradient). An opacity edit changes only the opacity: it does not sort.",
